                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[b]In a nutshell:[/b]\nMeh. Boring, short, and not worth it. Not much else to say.\n\n[b]The [strike]Long[/strike] Less Brief Version:[/b]\nI don't think it's worth wasting time picking this one apart too much. So here's a basic rundown:\n\nPlot is your standard \"evil thing kidnapping people from town\" story. Bland and predictable at best.\n\nFlavor text and written dialogue (no VOs) were okay, but nothing special. No glaring errors other than one or two misspelled HOG items.\n\nThe art is dark and muddy, with fuzzy details. It's not always clear what's interactable, so if you're not on easy mode (with annoying hint sparkles every 2 seconds) you'll be relying on blind clicking, hints, and map travel a lot - especially with the amount of backtracking. Hints seem to auto-trigger if you open the map too often without moving. I'm not sure how I feel about that.\n\nHOGs are not great. Again, dark colors palettes with fuzzy details. There are only a handful of scenes, and at least 3 of them repeat.\n\nPuzzles are infrequent, basic, and very easy.\n\nThe P&C item usage is frustrating. This is one of the more painful HOPAs where you find a tool that's technically perfect for the problem presented to you (ex. you have a pickaxe and come upon a chunk of ice something is stuck in), but that tool won't work. Instead you need to go out of your way and run backtracking circles until you find some other very specific item to solve the problem instead (ex. a pot of water to heat up and then pour on the ice). It happens often, and it's not very fun.\n\nThere's a bit of a \"morphing object\" style hunt, where you have to find doodles of suns that fade in and out of sight in non-puzzle/HOG areas. The only explanation is on the title screen if you happen to click on the locked \"Extras\" button. But nothing in-game shows them as an actual goal until you click one and see the #/20 counter pop up, so it's very easy to miss most of them. I certainly didn't find all 20, but I have zero interest in going back to find the rest. \n\nNo widescreen support. Not even black bars, just stretching.\n\n[h1]TL;DR: You can very safely skip this one.[/h1]",
